                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game needs work. Unfortunately it is being compared to Vanishing Realms which is a lot to live up to as one of the top games on the vive. I'm very interested to see this go further, but things needs to be fixed before it goes anywhere.\n\n1. Combat needs reworking. Swords feels floaty, specially the first sword you get. The flame one for some reason feels better. \n2. Both sword and shield suffer from getting stuck on the environment.\n3. One of the biggest problems and frustration was the game not always blocking attacks with the shield.\n4. I'm not a fan of the blackout screen when getting hit. I think a flash of red would work better.\n5. Teleporting needs work. I'm not sure the reason behind charging to teleport. It just doesn't seem fluid.\n6. Lastly, i found interesting that when you die, the game asks you to press F5 to retry. This is a room scale vr game not played with a keyboard. It breaks the immersion if you have to take off the headset to go to your keyboard. \n\nOn the plus side, it has great graphics and environment so far and it's not another wave shooter.",
